## Key label facts
* Pathway label is spelled exactly `Gardening` (capital G, one token) in
  `temporal_trends_contingency_table.csv` (column `pathway`) and in
  `invasion_success_pathways.csv` (column `intro.pathway`). Other levels: `AgriForest`, `Unintentional`.
* `invaded_niche_pathways.csv` has NO pathway string column: pathway is encoded as count
  columns `n.gard`, `n.unint`, `n.agfo`, with `n.gard + n.unint + n.agfo == n.total` in 632/632 rows.
* `intro.pathway` counts: Gardening 42, Unintentional 30, AgriForest 9
  (77 unique species; after dropping `duplicated==TRUE`: 39 / 29 / 9).
* `habitat` has exactly 10 levels, no NA: Scrublands 106, Croplands 92, Coniferous forests 77,
  Broad-leaved forests 68, Urban 65, Riparian 61, Rock outcrops 57, Meadows 39, Wetlands 38, Coastal 29.
* `habitat.range` (species table) is integer 1-7 with NO NA, contrary to the metadata text.
* Tree tip labels: 21 in tree but not in species table; 2 in table but not in tree
  (`Opuntia_ficus-indica`, `Opuntia_ficus-indica2`).

## Duplicates
77 unique `Scientific_name` in 81 rows. The 4 rows flagged `duplicated==TRUE` are the same
species repeated with a DIFFERENT pathway, all other traits identical:
Eucalyptus camaldulensis (AgriForest/Gardening), Opuntia ficus-indica (AgriForest/Gardening),
Oxalis debilis (Gardening/Unintentional), Populus deltoides (AgriForest/Gardening).

## Unit of observation
`invaded_niche_pathways.csv` = one row per plot (632 unique lon/lat pairs, no repeated plots).
Totals: n.gard 169, n.unint 289, n.agfo 23, n.total 481; 441/632 plots have n.total == 0.
No species names in that file, so plot-level pathway counts cannot be re-derived from the
species table (no join key) - it is already aggregated by pathway.

## Preview diagnostics (not the final analysis)
* share n.gard/n.total by habitat: Broad-leaved forests 1.000 (only 4 records), Coniferous 0.875 (8),
  Wetlands 0.558, Coastal 0.535, Scrublands 0.400 (5), Riparian 0.365, Meadows 0.308,
  Urban 0.298, Croplands 0.185, Rock outcrops 0.000 (1).
* occupancy (plots with >=1 gardening species / all plots): Wetlands 50.0%, Urban 47.7%,
  Coastal 44.8%, Riparian 36.1%, Croplands 20.7%, Coniferous 6.5%, Meadows 7.7%,
  Broad-leaved 4.4%, Scrublands 1.9%, Rock outcrops 0.0%.
* chi2 habitat x (gard vs rest) on records: 48.83, p=1.79e-7, dof=9, min expected 0.35 (sparse).
* chi2 on plot occupancy: 89.96, p=1.66e-15. Kruskal-Wallis on n.gard per plot: H=140.7, p=7.3e-26.

## Planned approach (awaiting approval)
Primary dataset: invaded_niche_pathways.csv. Metrics: share, occupancy, intensity (mean n.gard/plot)
+ concentration of the 169 gardening records. Tests: exact/simulated contingency test,
Kruskal-Wallis, quasi-binomial GLM n.gard ~ habitat (weights n.total), optional urban/elevation covariates.
Species table used as secondary evidence (habitat.range by pathway); temporal table as context only.
